 "decision_rule": {
  "text": "Controls: per-curve two-sample KS between null streams (draws 0-99 vs 100-199); the gate passes iff the count of curves with p < 0.05 is <= the 99th percentile of Binomial(#curves, 0.05); positive control u >= 0.95 on >= 90% of curves; otherwise INVALID. Cells: DETECTS iff all 3 class curves are beyond 5-95% in one direction at >= 2 of the sizes 10, 12, 14 and the paired ordinary curves are not all extreme in that direction; else BLIND. Overdispersion: X = #(u <= 0.05 or u >= 0.95) among the 90 extra ordinary curves; OVERDISPERSED iff P(Binomial(90, 0.10) >= X) < 0.01, else CALIBRATED.",
